[["text","LESSON 26 / 31 • ADDITIONAL INTERVIEW TOPIC"],["heading","26. BFS and DFS data structures"],["text","English: BFS uses a queue; DFS uses a stack or recursion."],["sinhala","","සිංහල: BFS level අනුවෙ යනවො. DFS එක path එකක් දිගට යනවො.",325],["text","Real-world example: Network reachability"],["code","BFS: A,B,C,D | DFS: A,B,D,C"],["code","Example tree A->B,C; B->D"],["heading","Java example / illustration"],["code","Deque<String> q = new ArrayDeque<>();\nq.offer(\"A\"); // BFS frontier\nDeque<String> s = new ArrayDeque<>();\ns.push(\"A\"); // DFS frontier"],["heading","Complexity and trade-offs"],["text","O(V+E) time with adjacency list; O(V) extra space."],["heading","Interview question"],["heading","Which finds shortest unweighted paths?"],["text","BFS."],["heading","Quick practice"],["text","Explain this concept aloud, trace the example, and describe when you would choose this"],["text","structure over an alternative."]]